change_type: instructions+docs+code   changelog: Watch several sites: vercel.projects and ga4.properties take lists in place of the singular keys, which still work. Each Vercel project is polled separately with its own alert state; a 0.1.1 state file carries over to the first project. The GA4 digest gets one section per property, and a failing property no longer holds back the rest.

### CHANGELOG.md  [docs]
+ ## [0.2.0] - 2026-10-14
+ ### Added
+ - **The Vercel and GA4 modules watch more than one site.** `vercel.projects`
+   takes a list of projects in place of `vercel.project`, and `ga4.properties` a
+   list of properties in place of `ga4.property`; the singular forms still work.
+   Each Vercel project is polled with its own query and keeps its own alert
+   state, so one site's errors neither raise nor clear another's alert. The GA4
+   digest gets one section per property, and a failing property no longer holds
+   back the rest. Uptime already took one watch per URL.
+ ### Changed
+ - **Vercel state is kept per project.** A state file written by 0.1.1 is read
+   back and handed to the first configured project, so upgrading neither repeats
+   an alert nor forgets an outstanding one.
+ - **`vercel-watch` saves its state even when it exits 2.** With several
+   projects, a configuration problem on one must not stop another's alert from
+   being remembered as sent.

### README.md  [docs]
+ To watch several sites, name them all with `projects` instead of `project`, for
+ example `"projects": ["my-project", "my-other-project"]`. Each project is polled
+ with its own query and keeps its own alert state, so errors on one site neither
+ raise nor clear an alert for another, and every alert names its project. The
+ `errors` and `budget` settings apply to all of them, and one account- or
+ team-scoped token covers them all.
+ For several sites, use `"properties": ["123456789", "987654321"]` instead of
+ `property`. The digest then has one section per property, and a property that
+ fails is reported in the run log without holding back the others.

### SETUP.md  [docs]
+ ```
+ ```json
+ For more than one site, list them under `projects` instead of `project`:
+ { "vercel": { "enabled": true, "projects": ["my-project", "my-other-project"] } }
+ Each project is polled separately and keeps its own alert state. Uptime needs no
+ equivalent: add one entry per URL to `uptime.watches`.
+ For several sites, write `"properties": ["123456789", "987654321"]` instead of
+ `property`; the digest gets one section per property.

